.           PHILADELPHIA ALTERNATE SYSTEMS USER GROUP
.                  http://www.phillyos2.org
  
The Philadelphia Alternate Systems User Group (PASUG), formerly
The Philadelphia OS/2 User Group, invites all interested computer
users to attend the March monthly meeting:
  
.              ***  MARCH MEETING AGENDA  ***
.      **  InCharge Financial Management Program  **
.                  **  LindowsOS Demo  **
  
SHORT PRESENTATION: Come See LindowsOS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Good news! Arrangements have been confirmed for the loan of a
LindowsOS computer, the widely discussed and publicized system
marketed by WalMart. David Moskowitz will conduct a live demo
and discussion of its major features.
  
MAIN PRESENTATION: InCharge Financial Management Program
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Doug Leach will conduct a presentation/demo of InCharge financial
management program for OS/2, a full-function personal & small
business financial management system which is available from
Spitfire Software. InCharge was originally written for OS/2 as a
native alternative to Quicken or MS Money. A Windows version is
also now available. There is complete feature equivalence, as
well as data compatibility, between the two versions.
  
InCharge supports an unlimited number of sets of books, multiple
currencies, multiple year budgeting, internet banking, and
securities & brokerage account management. InCharge also contains
a complete payables/receivables system which tracks bills & loans
in real time. For small business, InCharge provides billing and
invoicing as well as order entry and sales analysis.
  
Doug's presentation will cover the following items:
 - Creation and setup up of sets of books
 - Account management
 - Creation & setup of typical bills & transactions we all deal
   with on a regular basis.
 - Importing internet banking data.
 - Setup and creation of invoices for customers.
 - Setup and management of securities accounts.
- - - - -
  
Other agenda items include announcements, news, Q&A session and
raffles. The usual free refreshments will also be available.
  
Mark the date and time: Thursday, March 27th at 7:00pm.
PASUG meetings are open and free for all users, their guests and
others interested in learning about OS/2, Linux, other OS's and
associated technologies. We have a very full agenda and a tight
schedule. Please be on time promptly by 7:00pm to avoid missing
out on the earlier parts of the meeting.
  
.           **   WE SUPPORT OPEN STANDARDS   **
  
PASUG meetings are held at Bryn Mawr Community Center, next to
the Ludington Library, at the corner of Lancaster and Bryn Mawr
Aves, Bryn Mawr, PA. Meetings are scheduled on the 4th THURSDAY
of each month, except the 3rd THURSDAY in Nov. and Dec.
  
Directions to the Bryn Mawr Community Center (BMCC) and other
useful information about the PASUG activities may be found on
our web site at http://www.phillyos2.org, or contact U/G Leader
Larry Lavins: llavins@worldnet.att.net, or phone (215) 878-9608.
- -

